                <pb facs="0362" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg296"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00/3204: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-02T13:00:00-05:00">July 2, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. Department’s telegram No. 49 of June 21, 2 p.m. Could Department inform me
                    whether any decision has been reached and if so whether the announcement is to
                    be made following the meeting of the two Presidents.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
